# Credit Card Transactions Analysis | Python, SQL Server & Power BI

## Project Overview

This project analyzes **1,296,675 credit card transactions** to identify fraud patterns, evaluate customer spending behavior, and generate business insights.

The project demonstrates an end-to-end data analytics workflow using Python for data extraction, transformation, and cleaning (ETL), Microsoft SQL Server for data analysis, and Power BI for interactive dashboards.

**Project Objectives:**
- Analyze over 1.29 million credit card transactions.
- Identify fraudulent and legitimate transactions.
- Examine spending trends by category, state, and time.
- Calculate key fraud metrics and transaction statistics.
- Develop interactive Power BI dashboards.
- Provide data-driven business recommendations.

## Dataset Description

The dataset contains **1,296,675 records and 24 original columns**.

Key fields include:

| Column | Description |
|---|---|
| trans_date_trans_time | Transaction date and time |
| cc_num | Credit card account identifier |
| merchant | Merchant associated with transaction |
| category | Merchant spending category |
| amt | Transaction amount |
| gender | Customer gender |
| city | Customer city |
| state | Customer state |
| job | Customer occupation |
| dob | Customer date of birth |
| trans_num | Unique transaction identifier |
| is_fraud | Fraud indicator (1 = Fraud, 0 = Legitimate) |

The full dataset is not included in this repository because of its large size. The project includes code, analysis, documentation, and dashboard materials.

